# Auto commit and push

When you finish implementing requested work (features, fixes, refactors, migrations):

1. Create a git commit for the relevant changes (follow the repo's commit-message style; use a HEREDOC).
2. Push to the tracked remote branch (`git push -u origin HEAD` if needed).
3. Do this without waiting for an explicit "commit" / "push" request.

Still apply normal git safety: never force-push main/master, never amend pushed commits unless explicitly asked, never skip hooks, never commit secrets, and never update git config.
